  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Core Rulebook</i></p><p><i>See also: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Feats\" title=\"Feats\">Feats</a></i></p><p>You can avoid attacks made against your <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vehicle\">Vehicle</a>.</p><p><b>Prerequisite:</b> <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Trained\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Trained\">Trained</a> in <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pilot\" title=\"Pilot\">Pilot</a></p><p><b>Effect:</b> Once per round (as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Reaction\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Reaction\">Reaction</a>), when you are piloting a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vehicle\">Vehicle</a> or <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Starship\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Starship\">Starship</a>, you may negate a weapon hit by making a successful <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pilot\" title=\"Pilot\">Pilot</a> check. The DC of the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Skill_Check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Skill Check\">Skill Check</a> is equal to the result of the attack roll you wish to negate. In addition, while you are piloting a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vehicle\">Vehicle</a>, you are considered proficient with pilot-operated <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle_Weapons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vehicle Weapons\">Vehicle Weapons</a>.</p>",
